  "result": "```json\n{\n  \"smpl.ordering.PropertyHelper\": {\n    \"summary\": \"A utility class for loading and accessing application configuration properties from the classpath. The class provides static methods to load properties from property files, specifically designed to work with 'application.properties'. Key features include: (1) `getPropValues(String propFileName)` - loads properties from a specified file on the classpath using the ClassLoader, throwing FileNotFoundException if the file is not found; (2) `getProperties()` - returns the cached Properties object that was loaded during class initialization; (3) A static initializer block that automatically loads 'application.properties' when the class is first loaded, falling back to an empty Properties object if loading fails. The class maintains a static field `s_props` to cache the loaded properties for reuse. Note: There is a potential bug in `getPropValues` where the properties are loaded before checking if the inputStream is null, which could cause a NullPointerException.\",\n    \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/PropertyHelper.java\"\n  }\n}\n```",
